                        Braces can fix many asymmetries — but not all. The answer depends on whether the asymmetry is dental (in the teeth) or skeletal (in the jaw bones). A specialist exam with imaging is the only reliable way to find out which one you have, and what combination of orthodontics and orthognathic surgery will give you a stable, lasting result.
